speechtext:
That debate lasted several days, but it was a very important measure and surely there can be no criticism of the fact that the debate lasted so long. Then there was the wheat legislation, which also took considerable time in this house. I was much intrigued, if I may use that word, by the remarks of the hon. member for Lake Centre (Mr. Diefenbaker), who criticized the government severely, in his impassioned manner, because of its lack of economy. "Why are you not saving money," he said. "Look at your expenditures; look at the taxation the country is paying." But what was the attitude of the hon. member for Lake Centre when the wheat legislation was before the house? If he will look up Hansard and read his remarks at that time he will see that his whole criticism of the government was that we were not spending nearly enough money
Interim Supply Bill

for the relief of the wheat farmers. And he had a very good seconder in his colleague, the hon. member for Qu'Appelle (Mr. Perley)

I move the following
amendments:
Clause 1, lines 9 to 12: strike out paragraph (a) and substitute therefor the following,
"(a) 'corporation' means the Bank of Canada, every bank to which the Bank Act applies or to which the Quebec Savings Banks Act applies, and each and every of the following carrying on business in Canada, namely, every railway, express, telegraph and telephone company (except a street railway and tramway company),

insurance company or society, trust company and loan company (except a company subject to the provisions of part II of the Small Loans Act, 1939);
(b) 'government' means the government of Canada or of any province of Canada and includes any department, commission, board or branch of any such government;"
2.	Clause 1, line 13: strike out "(b)" and substitute therefor "(c)";
3. Clause 1, line 17: strike out the word "bank" and substitute therefor the words, "government or corporation";
4. Clause 1, line 21: strike out the word "original";
M 5- Clause 1, lino 21: strike out the words "a bank" and substitute therefor the words, "any government or corporation";
6.	Clause 1, line 25: strike out all the words after "any" to the end of line 27 and substitute the words "government or corporation";
6a. Clause 1, page 2, line 2: strike out the word "original";
7.	Clause 1, page 2, lines 4 and 5: strike out the words "bank, department, commission, board or branch" and substitute therefor the words "government or corporation";
8.	Clause 1, page 2, lines 9 and 10: strike out the words "bank, department, commission, board or branch" and substitute therefor the words "government or corporation";
9.	Clause 1, page 2, line 14: strike out the words "bank, department, commission, board or branch" and substitute therefor the words, "government or corporation".
